# Reduck script quality

Local mirrors live in `web.snapchat.com/scripts/<slug>/{script.js,meta.json}`. Reduck address stays `@handle/web.snapchat.com/<slug>` (not under `scripts/` on the server).

## Contracts
- Validate required `args` up front; throw clear errors.
- Return a stable object shape every time (counts, flags, arrays — never naked `undefined`).
- Set `loggedIn` and `sideEffects` honestly in `meta.json`.
- One script = one job. Chain via caller args; do not mega-script.

## Resilience (Anybuddy lessons)
- Prefer finite timeouts. Never wait forever for optional UI.
- Empty lists and not-found → **structured success** (`count: 0`, `opened: false` / `notFound: true`), not a 45s timeout.
- Logged-out → clear `{ loggedIn: false, ... }` or an explicit error — document the choice in QA.
- Insert short delays between open-chat and scrape to stay human-paced.

## Selectors
- Prefer role/text locators when stable; fall back carefully for Snapchat’s SPA.
- Virtualized lists: only scrape visible rows up to `limit`; document the cap.

## Tests
- Every script needs cases in `web.snapchat.com/tests/cases.json` (happy + empty/not-found).
- After suite runs, write `benchmarks/latest.md` via `tests/run-benchmark.mjs`.
